From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 14:53:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: don't wait for the threaded IRQ handler under
 core->lock

iris_vpu_power_off() calls disable_irq(), which waits for a running
threaded handler. All its callers hold core->lock: iris_core_deinit()
(remove and the sys error handler), the iris_core_init() error path, and
runtime suspend/resume. The threaded handler iris_hfi_isr_handler() takes
core->lock first thing. If an interrupt arrives just before power off,
the two wait for each other:

  rmmod qcom_iris
    iris_remove -> iris_core_deinit    mutex_lock(&core->lock)
      iris_fw_unload
      iris_vpu_power_off -> disable_irq -> synchronize_irq   (waits for irq/281-iris)
  irq/281-iris
    iris_hfi_isr_handler               mutex_lock(&core->lock)  (waits for rmmod)
  -> hung task panic

Seen on a Lenovo Legion Tab Gen 5 (Kaanapali): rmmod right after a decode
session, and console-ramoops showed both stacks.

The wait protected only the handler's register access
(iris_vpu_clear_interrupt()) on powered-off hardware. The queue reads in
the response handler already take core->lock and bail out unless the core
is in IRIS_CORE_INIT. So track the power state under core->lock, let the
handler skip the hardware when it is off, and use disable_irq_nosync() in
iris_vpu_power_off().

The IRQ disable depth does not change. When the handler bails out, it
undoes only the disable_irq_nosync() of iris_hfi_isr(); the disable from
power off stays until iris_vpu_power_on() enables the IRQ again.
iris_core_deinit() calls synchronize_irq() after it drops the lock, so
remove still waits for the handler before it tears down.

Fixes: b9c2215bdedc ("media: qcom: iris: use disable_irq() during power-off")
Signed-off-by: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>

[ from github.com/joonhoekim/tb323fu-linux kernel/patches/0112 at commit
  1f4d59006b0f (added 2026-09-30); the Lenovo TB323FU (Kaanapali) port ]
[ upstream author: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>; picked for the iceland kernel q89s ]
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_core.c       | 3 +++
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_core.h       | 1 +
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_common.c | 6 ++++++
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vpu_common.c | 9 ++++++++-
 4 files changed, 18 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_core.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_core.c
index d558475986ff..32b7639a4e65 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_core.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_core.c
@@ -29,6 +29,9 @@ void iris_core_deinit(struct iris_core *core)
 	}
 	mutex_unlock(&core->lock);
 
+	/* let a handler that was waiting for core->lock finish */
+	synchronize_irq(core->irq);
+
 	if (!ret)
 		pm_runtime_put_sync(core->dev);
 }
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_core.h b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_core.h
index 3e4cf652bf39..293d0a4fa70a 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_core.h
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_core.h
@@ -88,6 +88,7 @@ struct iris_core {
 	struct device				*dev;
 	void __iomem				*reg_base;
 	int					irq;
+	bool					hw_powered;
 	struct v4l2_device			v4l2_dev;
 	struct video_device			*vdev_dec;
 	struct video_device			*vdev_enc;
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_common.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_common.c
index de4d53f31983..e120b6fa8f4a 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_common.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_common.c
@@ -109,6 +109,12 @@ irqreturn_t iris_hfi_isr_handler(int irq, void *data)
 		return IRQ_NONE;
 
 	mutex_lock(&core->lock);
+	if (!core->hw_powered) {
+		/* powered off meanwhile: undo iris_hfi_isr()'s disable only */
+		mutex_unlock(&core->lock);
+		enable_irq(irq);
+		return IRQ_HANDLED;
+	}
 	pm_runtime_mark_last_busy(core->dev);
 	iris_vpu_clear_interrupt(core);
 	mutex_unlock(&core->lock);
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vpu_common.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vpu_common.c
index 243bd845349f..3dc1580d92b1 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vpu_common.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vpu_common.c
@@ -239,8 +239,14 @@ void iris_vpu_power_off(struct iris_core *core)
 	core->iris_platform_data->vpu_ops->power_off_controller(core);
 	iris_unset_icc_bw(core);
 
+	/*
+	 * Callers hold core->lock, which the threaded handler takes too:
+	 * don't wait for it here. It sees hw_powered == false and leaves the
+	 * hardware alone.
+	 */
+	core->hw_powered = false;
 	if (!iris_vpu_watchdog(core, core->intr_status))
-		disable_irq(core->irq);
+		disable_irq_nosync(core->irq);
 }
 
 int iris_vpu_power_on_controller(struct iris_core *core)
@@ -521,6 +527,7 @@ int iris_vpu_power_on(struct iris_core *core)
 
 	core->iris_platform_data->vpu_ops->interrupt_init(core);
 	core->intr_status = 0;
+	core->hw_powered = true;
 	enable_irq(core->irq);
 
 	return 0;
